---
// The IDS station's twist, as two comic frames: the poisoning finding, then the defence.
import RoughFrame from './marks/RoughFrame.astro';
---

<div class="twist" aria-label="The twist">
  <figure>
    <RoughFrame class="cell" seed={41} w={240} h={200}>
      <div class="pair">
        <img src="/characters/intruder/idle-still.svg" alt="The Intruder tiptoeing up with a lockpick" width="256" height="256" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/characters/honeybot/idle-still.svg" alt="Honeybot on its honeypot, not noticing" width="256" height="256" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </RoughFrame>
    <figcaption class="hand">the twist: it slips poison into the honey. auto-labelled honeypot data can poison the IDS.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure>
    <RoughFrame class="cell" seed={43} w={240} h={200}>
      <div class="pair">
        <img src="/characters/honeybot/action-still.svg" alt="Honeybot slamming the lid down on the jar, the poison bottle knocked over" width="256" height="256" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </RoughFrame>
    <figcaption class="hand">Honeybot caps how much of the jar gets eaten. that cap is the defence.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>

<style>
  .twist {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .twist :global(.cell) {
    padding: 8px;
  }

  .pair {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .pair img {
    width: 50%;
    max-width: 110px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .pair img:only-child {
    width: 70%;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }
</style>
